WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Bam!

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.609
(epic music plays)

00:00:02.609 --> 00:00:03.442
(speaks foreign language)

00:00:03.442 --> 00:00:04.698
(inaudible whining)

00:00:04.698 --> 00:00:06.358
- [Brunette Girl] This is crazy!

00:00:06.358 --> 00:00:08.355
- I don't understand anything!

00:00:08.355 --> 00:00:09.783
- I can't believe she's Asian.

00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:11.861
(laughter)

00:00:11.861 --> 00:00:15.321
(classical violin music)

00:00:15.321 --> 00:00:16.621
- We're playing mahjong

00:00:16.621 --> 00:00:17.840
(speaks foreign language)

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:18.862
That means "play mahjong."

00:00:18.862 --> 00:00:21.748
So mahjong is a really old
game that originated in China.

00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:24.806
It's one of the best games
that I've ever played.

00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:29.288
- It looks like chess and
checkers and cards combined.

00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:30.635
- I've never even seen it played

00:00:30.635 --> 00:00:32.910
but I know it's supposed to be really fun

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.954
and there's a lot of yelling involved.

00:00:34.954 --> 00:00:36.254
- If you're losing, yes.

00:00:36.254 --> 00:00:38.042
- I really don't know what this game is.

00:00:38.042 --> 00:00:40.445
I've only seen it played
in Chinese dramas.

00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:42.349
- The best way to start learning is

00:00:42.349 --> 00:00:44.195
to understand what the tiles are.

00:00:44.195 --> 00:00:45.499
You have three types of tiles.

00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:48.832
You have suits, honors, and bonus, okay?

00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:53.226
So usually we play on a square table

00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:54.664
because it's just easier.

00:00:54.664 --> 00:00:56.591
So now we're going to wash them

00:00:56.591 --> 00:00:59.489
and everyone turn them
over onto their green.

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:00.572
So wash them.

00:01:01.478 --> 00:01:02.708
Like, rotate it.

00:01:02.708 --> 00:01:03.541
Oh sh-t.

00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:05.506
The grandmas, the aunts,
everyone will play

00:01:05.506 --> 00:01:06.899
this around the table.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.200
The kids will hang out

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.928
and they would just gossip over stuff.

00:01:10.928 --> 00:01:12.472
Yeah, it was part of growing up.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.688
There was like, five sets of
mahjong in my grandma's house

00:01:15.688 --> 00:01:19.321
and she invited every human over to play.

00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:21.029
Everyone has a version of mahjong.

00:01:21.029 --> 00:01:24.330
This is gonna be pretty
basic like, Chinese version.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.927
- It's just pretty much
like a matching game almost.

00:01:26.927 --> 00:01:28.030
- It is a matching game.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.539
- Is it like that one game Bullsh-t?

00:01:31.539 --> 00:01:34.956
- [Brunette] So I take two, you take two.

00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:38.040
You take two.
- [Guy With The Glasses] Okay.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.259
- You take two.

00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:40.092
- [Blonde Girl] It has to be the next one?

00:01:40.092 --> 00:01:40.925
- [Brunette Girl] Yep.

00:01:40.925 --> 00:01:42.518
Faster guys, quick status, yep.

00:01:42.518 --> 00:01:43.853
Everyone's fast in this game.

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:46.495
- [Guy With The Hat] Got it, got it.

00:01:46.495 --> 00:01:48.461
- Okay, so you can either choose

00:01:48.461 --> 00:01:49.680
- (inaudible)

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.108
- [Brunette Girl] That's a dragon.

00:01:52.108 --> 00:01:55.775
- [Guy With A Hat] Girl!
What are you doin'?

00:01:57.955 --> 00:01:58.788
- What do I do now?

00:01:58.788 --> 00:02:00.705
- Nothing! Now he goes.

00:02:05.196 --> 00:02:07.904
- [Guy With A Hat] Two of a kind is good.

00:02:07.904 --> 00:02:10.621
(laughter)

00:02:10.621 --> 00:02:13.788
(inaudible muttering)

00:02:14.777 --> 00:02:18.027
- Ha! Bam!
- [Brunette Girl] He's crazy!

00:02:20.919 --> 00:02:22.138
- [Guy With A Hat] I feel
like I'm getting in touch

00:02:22.138 --> 00:02:25.191
with my Asian heritage
and I am winning at it.

00:02:25.191 --> 00:02:26.024
Yes!

00:02:26.944 --> 00:02:28.488
- So Mallory, when did you start playing?

00:02:28.488 --> 00:02:30.683
- I learned probably early on, like seven.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.517
My grandma and my mom would talk about it

00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:33.933
and say "this is this" and "that's that"

00:02:33.933 --> 00:02:36.255
you have to match them and
it's like a matching game.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:39.437
But I never played probably
until I was in college.

00:02:39.437 --> 00:02:40.284
- How come?

00:02:40.284 --> 00:02:44.568
- My grandma died so then
mahjong kind of left with her.

00:02:44.568 --> 00:02:47.053
- Wait! Wait wait wait! Did I win?

00:02:47.053 --> 00:02:48.877
- Do you have pairs? And a--

00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:50.835
(tiles clatter)

00:02:50.835 --> 00:02:52.237
- No!

00:02:52.237 --> 00:02:53.782
- Hide that two four!

00:02:53.782 --> 00:02:57.450
It has to be Pong, Kong,
or Chow and then one pair.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.273
Also, you should say "mahjong."

00:02:59.273 --> 00:03:00.523
- Mahjong! Why?

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:03.623
- It's like Uno.

00:03:03.623 --> 00:03:07.290
So basically you have
one last hand to play.

00:03:08.816 --> 00:03:09.649
F-ck.

00:03:09.649 --> 00:03:11.441
- Yeah. Suck it.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:13.925
Wait wait. I might have three.
- You know what they say?

00:03:13.925 --> 00:03:14.947
- Three right?

00:03:14.947 --> 00:03:16.456
- Mahjong. Oh sh-t.

00:03:16.456 --> 00:03:18.163
- Ah! You have mahjong?

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:20.032
Wait, does that mean you won?
- [Brunette Girl] Yeah

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.017
(cries of protest)

00:03:22.017 --> 00:03:22.985
- Okay this game is rigged.

00:03:22.985 --> 00:03:25.472
(peppy piano music)

00:03:25.472 --> 00:03:28.014
- So fun 'cause I almost won.

00:03:28.014 --> 00:03:32.097
- Not gonna lie it was
hard but it was fun, yeah.

00:03:32.987 --> 00:03:34.891
How can you say that you did a bad job

00:03:34.891 --> 00:03:36.319
when you get three white dragons?

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:39.210
- [Guy With A Hat] I
definitely feel more connected

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.323
with my Chinese side
'cause I remember learning

00:03:41.323 --> 00:03:43.157
these Chinese characters
when I was in school

00:03:43.157 --> 00:03:45.027
and it totally reminded me of that stuff.

00:03:45.027 --> 00:03:46.327
- I had a great time.

00:03:46.327 --> 00:03:49.218
I would love to invite
friends over, gossip, play it.

00:03:49.218 --> 00:03:50.890
- [Guy With Hat] Yeah, that sounds fun.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:53.862
- [Guy With Glasses] Let's just
all hang out and play this.

00:03:53.862 --> 00:03:55.046
- [Blonde Girl] Yeah, I'm down.

00:03:55.046 --> 00:03:58.046
- If there's alcohol, I'll be there.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:04.241
You gave me the easy ones?

00:04:04.241 --> 00:04:06.029
You gave me the easy ones?

00:04:06.029 --> 00:04:07.112
These Asians?

